cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite both this software and the paper listed under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "liv_zones: Spatial organelle segmentation and mapping pipeline for fluorescence microscopy"
abstract: >-
  liv_zones is a Python pipeline for spatial organellomics analysis of
  fluorescence microscopy images. It segments cells and organelles
  (mitochondria, lipid droplets, peroxisomes) from multi-channel confocal
  z-stacks using Cellpose, extracts per-organelle and per-cell morphological
  features, and maps them spatially along anatomical tissue axes
  (portal-to-central vein in liver; endocrine/exocrine regions in pancreas).
  The pipeline covers image preprocessing (cropping, z-stack max projection,
  image correction filters), cell filtering, feature extraction, and
  generation of spatial trend plots. It supports multi-tissue analysis and
  is extensible to new tissue types via community forks.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-09"
license: MIT
